%description:

Tcp.minshallNagle:off -- the short end of a write waits while full-sized segments are not acknowledged.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "false: the Nagle algorithm of RFC 9293 section 3.7.4, where a small
segment waits while any data is not acknowledged".

The classes: off (false, the default), on (true; LinuxTcp). The code: with Minshall, only an
earlier small segment that is not acknowledged holds a small segment
(TcpConnection::sendData()). This test separates "off" from "on".

Host under test: host1, with Nagle, which writes 3000 bytes at once: two full-sized segments
of 1448 bytes and an end of 104 bytes. The links have a delay of 10 ms, so the round trip is
40 ms. Observation: level 1, the end of 104 bytes goes after the first ACK, about 40 ms after
the first segment.

%# parameter: Tcp.minshallNagle
%# class: off
%# value: false
%# key: *.host1.tcp.minshallNagle
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpMinshallNagleOff")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("the first data segment of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
              .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength && pk.dataLength < tcp.headerLength + 1448B")
              .describe("an early end of the write, after the first ACK")
              .within(0.03))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength && pk.dataLength < tcp.headerLength + 1448B")
             .describe("end of the write, after the first ACK")
             .within(0.02));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpMinshallNagleOff compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.minshallNagle = false    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 3000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpMinshallNagleOff: PASS
